## AI Pair Programming Standards

Cloud Burst uses AI pair programming to accelerate development while maintaining code quality and consistency.

### Communication Guidelines

When collaborating with AI assistants:

- **Be specific**: Provide clear requirements and context
- **Use incremental steps**: Break down complex tasks
- **Review generated code**: Verify correctness and style
- **Ask for explanations**: Understand the implementation
- **Provide feedback**: Help the AI improve
- **Consider performance**: Discuss optimization opportunities
- **Consider accessibility**: Ensure inclusive design
- **Consider mobile**: Ensure responsive implementation

### Code Generation Standards

AI-generated code should follow these standards:

- Use TypeScript with strict type checking
- Follow Next.js 14 App Router best practices
- Maintain consistent code style
- Include proper error handling
- Ensure accessibility compliance
- Follow security best practices
- Optimize for performance
- Support mobile devices

### Gallery Implementation Standards

When implementing gallery features:

- Use virtualization for large collections
- Implement progressive loading
- Optimize image loading and caching
- Support keyboard navigation
- Implement touch controls
- Support offline functionality
- Include analytics tracking
- Ensure responsive design

### Mobile Implementation Standards

When implementing mobile features:

- Use progressive enhancement
- Implement responsive design
- Optimize touch interactions
- Support offline functionality
- Monitor performance
- Consider battery impact
- Handle network changes
- Track analytics

### Analytics Implementation Standards

When implementing analytics features:

- Use real-time data processing
- Implement data aggregation
- Create accessible visualizations
- Support data export
- Optimize for mobile
- Handle offline scenarios
- Monitor performance
- Ensure security

## Example Implementations

### Gallery Component
```typescript
const GalleryGrid = () => {
  const { items, virtualizer } = useMasonryGrid({
    columnWidth: 300,
    gap: 16,
    items: photos,
  });

  return (
    <div ref={virtualizer.ref}>
      {items.map((item) => (
        <PhotoCard
          key={item.id}
          photo={item}
          loading="progressive"
          analytics={{
            track: true,
            category: 'gallery',
            action: 'view'
          }}
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

### Mobile Component
```typescript
const MobileGallery = () => {
  const { isOnline, networkType } = useNetwork();
  const { items, loadMore } = useInfiniteGallery({
    batchSize: 20,
    prefetch: networkType === '4g',
    offlineFirst: true
  });

  return (
    <div>
      <InfiniteScroll
        items={items}
        onLoadMore={loadMore}
        useWindowScroll
        threshold={500}
      >
        {(item) => (
          <PhotoCard
            key={item.id}
            photo={item}
            loading="progressive"
            offline={!isOnline}
          />
        )}
      </InfiniteScroll>
    </div>
  );
};
```

### Analytics Component
```typescript
const AnalyticsDashboard = () => {
  const { data, isLoading } = useRealTimeMetrics({
    interval: 5000,
    aggregation: 'sum',
    cache: true
  });

  return (
    <div>
      <MetricsChart
        data={data}
        loading={isLoading}
        type="line"
        responsive
        accessible
        exportable
      />
      <MetricsTable
        data={data}
        loading={isLoading}
        virtual
        sortable
        filterable
        exportable
      />
    </div>
  );
};
```

### RSVP Form Component
```typescript
const RsvpForm = ({ invitationToken }: { invitationToken: string }) => {
  const form = useForm<RsvpFormValues>({
    resolver: zodResolver(rsvpFormSchema),
    defaultValues: {
      status: 'pending',
      plusOne: false,
      dietaryRestrictions: '',
      notes: ''
    }
  });
  
  const { mutate, isLoading } = useSubmitRsvp();
  
  const onSubmit = (values: RsvpFormValues) => {
    mutate({ token: invitationToken, ...values });
  };
  
  return (
    <Form {...form}>
      <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
        <FormField
          control={form.control}
          name="status"
          render={({ field }) => (
            <FormItem>
              <FormLabel>Will you attend?</FormLabel>
              <RadioGroup
                onValueChange={field.onChange}
                defaultValue={field.value}
              >
                <RadioItem value="accepted">Yes, I'll be there</RadioItem>
                <RadioItem value="declined">No, I can't make it</RadioItem>
              </RadioGroup>
            </FormItem>
          )}
        />
        
        {/* Additional form fields */}
        
        <Button type="submit" disabled={isLoading}>
          {isLoading ? "Submitting..." : "Submit RSVP"}
        </Button>
      </form>
    </Form>
  );
};
```